Input: {"question": "What is the genre of \"Foul Play\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0443-28f5d549a306:d00", "start": 0, "end": 166, "text": "Foul Play (album) Foul Play is a 1981 album by reggae singer Dennis Brown, the first of three albums to be released as part of his international record deal with A&M."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0443-28f5d549a306:d00", "start": 167, "end": 337, "text": "The album features two tracks which have been described as \"two of the greatest roots cuts in major label history\", in \"The Existence of Jah\" and \"The World is Troubled\"."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0443-28f5d549a306:d00", "start": 338, "end": 530, "text": "The album was reissued on the Joe Gibbs label as a double-set with its follow-up, \"Love Has Found Its Way\", and with both of the other A&M albums on the double-CD set \"The Complete A&M Years\"."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0443-28f5d549a306:d00", "start": 531, "end": 546, "text": "The album mixed"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0443-28f5d549a306:d01", "start": 0, "end": 337, "text": "Professionals - backing vocals Technical Errol Thompson - engineer , mixing Larry Maxwell - executive producer Aaron Rapoport - photography References [ edit ] ^ Henderson , Alex `` Foul Play Review `` , Allmusic , Macrovision Corporation ^ a b Thompson , Dave ( 2002 ) Reggae & Caribbean Music , Backbeat Books , ISBN 0-87930-655-6 , p."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0443-28f5d549a306:d01", "start": 338, "end": 467, "text": "45 , 47 ^ Walker , Klive ( 2006 ) Dubwise : Reasoning from the Reggae Underground , Insomniac Press , ISBN 978-1-894663-96-0 , p."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0443-28f5d549a306:d01", "start": 468, "end": 530, "text": "220 Retrieved from `` https : //en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php ?"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ra